      "extract": "Let $J = \\cup_{k=0}^{n}J_k = \\cup_{k=0}^{n}(a_k, b_k)$ be a union of $n+1$ disjoint intervals in $\\mathbb{R}$. Consider the Fredholm determinant $$P_x= \\det \\left( 1 - K_{\\textrm{sine}}\\right),$$ where $K_{\\textrm{sine}}$ is the trace class operator in $L_2\\Bigl(J; dz\\Bigr)$ with kernel $$K_{\\textrm{sine}}(z,z') = \\frac{\\sin x(z-z')}{\\pi (z-z')}.$$ The determinant $P_x$ plays a central role in random matrix theory.",
